# getChannelMembersByIds + getTeamMembersByIds + getPublicChannelsByIdsForTeam + getAllRoles
# — 2026-09-04.
#
# name<TAB>file<TAB>from<TAB>to<TAB>suite<TAB>filter
#
# Stack-backed lines are filtered to the one parity module that exercises the route —
# `by_ids_lists` for the three by-ids routes, `roles` for `getAllRoles`. Leaving the filter off
# lets an unrelated suite decide the verdict.
#
# Two anchors need care. `crates/mm-api/src/channels.rs` holds several `body.push(b'\n');`, so
# each trailing-newline line carries its own handler's marshal error above it; and a relaxed SQL
# predicate must keep **every** bind parameter referenced — `pc.teamid IS NOT NULL` alone drops
# `$1` and sqlx then refuses to compile, which the harness reports as a fault rather than a catch.
# Hence the `OR ... IS NOT NULL` shape: always true, same placeholders.
#
# Two lines are not `api`. `tm-ids-empty-guard` is `store`: the guard it deletes is unreachable
# through api4, which answers `invalid_body_param` for an empty array long before the store is
# called, so its oracle is `db_team_members.rs` rather than the parity suite — the [D-151] shape,
# and it survived a whole api-suite run before the store test existed.
#
# The other is `unit`, not `api`: the parameter *name* in a 400 never reaches the wire
# (`AppError.params` is `json:"-"`, and our `message` is the untranslated id — [D-092]), so a
# cross-server test cannot see it. `malformed_channel_id_parameter` exists to give that name an
# in-process oracle; without it the mutation is the [D-149] shape and survives for a reason that
# is not a test gap.

